0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Title: Forecast demand before contacting the vendor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Action: Size real demand from utilization data first, then open the negotiation on usage before rate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Detail: Lindberg forecasts demand before sending the first email to the vendor, so the negotiation starts from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (usage rather than the vendor's proposed volume [FinOps Foundation - iIwpcQbBkmM @ 00:14:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (License harvesting is where the hard money gets clawed back, and the mechanics are already scripted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (Michelle Campos of the ServiceNow Community ranks integrations by strength: direct vendor integration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (first, SSO through Azure or Okta second, and custom open API last. The Salesforce playbook then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (auto-builds a software model and a reclaim rule with a 30-day inactivity threshold. Campos recommends) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (reviewing that threshold and possibly stretching it to 90 days [8mJc7j3DW28 @ 00:03:48]. In the live demo) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (that rule surfaced 572 reclaim candidates, which can be reclaimed one at a time, all at once, or on full) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (automation [8mJc7j3DW28 @ 00:05:14]. Scogo AI ran the same play against Microsoft 365 with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (natural-language prompt in Cira CLI, stripping Business Premium licenses from disabled and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (never-signed-in users. Out of 25 licenses, the available count jumped from 21 to 24. That is three seats) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (reclaimed, including one the presenter had missed, confirmed in the admin portal [hkNjUpPIx6M @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (00:02:27]. Procure IT's module hooks the same identity providers \(Azure Entra, Okta or G Suite\) to split) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (power users from light users. The renewal conversation therefore starts with a list of who does not need a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (seat [_PyR6G51QW4 @ 00:01:11]. Every one of these workflows runs on the same two inputs: an identity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (signal and an inactivity threshold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (The contract math is where these practitioners get brutally specific. Mason walks through the commitment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (shortfall at Roku. Commit $1M over 12 months, spend only $900K, and you owe the vendor $100K. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (escape hatch is a mini business case committing to $1.2M, which may get the shortfall forgiven) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm ([LF1AK1WypX0 @ 00:14:06]. The opposite failure bites too. Burn through prepaid funds at month nine and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (the discount ends, forcing an early renewal, which matters because some of those Roku discounts run over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (90% [LF1AK1WypX0 @ 00:15:42]. At the negotiating table, Mason asks for discounted overages, free) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (training and support, and an at-will termination clause carrying 30, 60 or 90 days' notice [LF1AK1WypX0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (00:25:11]. Reed bakes soft caps into a standard tech-contract framework originally built at UBS, complete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (with reporting clauses. Usage up to 20% over the cap is free in year one, and in year two the customer pays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (50% of the delta [hQDjTANIaTo @ 00:29:33]. That clause structure converts a surprise true-up into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (negotiated, predictable ramp. Together these levers turn every renewal from a vendor-driven event into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (buyer-scheduled one, with the shortfall, overage and exit terms written in well before anyone signs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (Rate versus usage is the sharpest piece of street math on the board, and it is where most negotiated wins) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (quietly evaporate. Lindberg's worked example is to buy 1,000 licenses up front and watch the rollout take a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (full year. Every gap between contracted and active licenses is pure waste. The effective rate, contract cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (divided by actual usage, can equal or exceed on-demand pricing, so procurement needs to hear that its) Tj ET
