BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Jobank warns, working-capital metrics look incredibly weak to any investor scrutinizing the books.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (The most common self-inflicted wound is booking the invoice as revenue. Ben Murray of The SaaS CFO) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (calls out companies that debit receivables and credit revenue for the full $12,000 annual subscription in one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (month instead of deferring it and pulling it in ratably [p4KgISWaH6s @ 00:05:05]. Concierge CPA's Big Tech) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (example drives the same point: $120,000 wired on January 1 is zero revenue that day and $10,000 a month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (thereafter, because revenue follows performance, not cash. Suresh Perryami of Accounting and Auditing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Hub lists three traps from a $600,000 Cloud Nova contract: never recognize a non-refundable $50,000 setup) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (fee on day one, never trust invoice prices over standalone selling prices, and always treat a $20,000-a-year) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (uptime SLA refund as variable consideration that must be formally assessed before locking the transaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (price [-5y55BOFAKA @ 00:05:48]. Cloud Nova only constrained that penalty to zero because historical data) Tj ET
